WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.867
By this point, you should recognize the main Pandas patterns used in everyday analysis.

00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:13.182
You should be comfortable creating and loading data frames, inspecting structure, selecting rows and columns,

00:00:13.182 --> 00:00:20.277
handling missing values and duplicates, converting types, cleaning text, working with dates, grouping data,

00:00:20.277 --> 00:00:25.147
building pivot tables, merging related tables, and validating results.

00:00:25.147 --> 00:00:30.782
You do not need expert knowledge of every Pandas feature.

00:00:30.782 --> 00:00:35.477
Professional skill means you can use the core patterns confidently, recognize when something looks wrong,

00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:42.613
and learn an unfamiliar method from the documentation when the project requires it.

00:00:43.184 --> 00:00:51.376
Module 11 will build on this foundation with more advanced Pandas patterns, richer transformations, reshaping,

00:00:51.376 --> 00:00:58.550
more complex grouped operations, time-based workflows, and performance-oriented techniques.
